Control Theory: Empirical vs Analytical Methods
Goal of Control Engineering
To design and build real physical systems to perform given tasks.
• Example: Design and install a heat exchanger to control the temperature and humidity of a large building.
• Empirical method: Determination of required capacity of exchanger from total volume and geographical location of the building.
• Replacement of the exchanger if not powerful enough to control the building’s environment.
• Relies heavily on the experience and repeated experimentation.
• Inadequate without the experience or infeasible experimentation because of high cost or risk.
• Examples of infeasible experimentation:
▲ Task of sending astronauts to the moon and bringing them back safely. ▲ Design of fusion control in nuclear power plants.
