Control Theory: System Definition
System
A collection of components that interact with one another and with their environment.
• A set of interconnected or interdependent components or parts that work together to achieve a common goal or purpose.
• Examples
▷ Human beings, mechanical devices, and an electrical switch.
▷ Plants, animals, the atmosphere, the stock market, and the political system.
▷ Aerospace systems like aircraft, helicopters, missiles, avionics, rocket engines, and so on.
• Assumptions always needed for the design and analysis of systems.
• Physical Model: An idealized physical system
• A system may be modeled or viewed differently depending on scenarios.
