What is a “Systems” View?
Example
A satellite may be considered a point mass object, a rigid body, or a flexible body, depending on the specific study intended.
• Building a model with reasonable accuracy requires gradual removal of idealized assumptions until a point of diminishing return is reached.
• Gain in accuracy of representations is not commensurate with the increased complexity of the computations needed.
• Physical model =⇒ Mathematical model
• A mathematical representation using appropriate physical laws
• Mathematical models may differ depending on the choice of variables, the coordinate system, etc.
• Aim to achieve high modeling accuracy
• A particular mathematical model that gives a greater insight into the governing dynamics and behavior of the system is typically deemed viable for a given application.
