Control Theory: Requirements
▷ What are the features of a well-designed control system?
▷ System must be stable.
▷ Stability: Think of it as a requirement mandating that the output of a system should be well-behaved when its input is well-behaved.
▷ Output must track the desired output (reference or command) with zero or small steady-state error.
▷ Transient response of the system must be acceptable.
▷ Effect of disturbance and measurement noise on the system’s response should be made as small as possible.
▷ Design should be robust to model uncertainties.
▷ Design should meet any constraints associated with the control input.
